---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  A plan task's `## Budgets` section: every budget the task owns, in full. `plan-task`
  includes it after the task's `## Why`, and `just check-plan` renders it alone from the
  task's `orchestrator.budgets` metadata to hold the task's body to that record.
variables:
  # llmlint: ignore-block[contracts_have_one_source_or_a_drift_gate] The `budgets` description restates in words the shape its own `schema` below states once, which the plan store holds every rendering to; `tests/e2e/planning/` renders a record breaking it and reads the refusal.
  budgets:
    description: >-
      One object per budget this task owns, or `[]` when it owns none, with exactly these
      keys. `id` (string, the budget's id in its budgets file). `name` (string, a short
      plain-English name on one line, at most 60 characters). `basis` (string, how solid
      the number is: `measured`, `arithmetic`, `design`, `published docs` or `estimate`).
      `repository` (string, the normalized origin `host/owner/name` of the repository the
      budget goes in). `file` (string, the repository-relative path of the `budgets.yaml`
      it goes in: `budgets.yaml` for a repo-wide budget, or a project's own file for a
      scoped one). `file_change` (string, `add`, `change` or `none`: what the task does
      to that file's entry). `measure` (string, what is measured, in words, as near as
      possible to where the product owner feels it, at the level the product owner
      tracks, and the breakdown its analysis reports in the onebudgetspec reporter's
      `detail`: the per-step, per-phase or per-operation figures and any second unit of
      the same concern, which are telemetry rather than budgets of their own).
      `inner_measure_reason` (string, why the measure is taken further inward than that,
      or `""` when it is not). `unit`
      (string), `direction` (string, `max` or `min`) and `threshold` (a finite number),
      each meaning what it means in onebudgetspec. `workload` (string, the realistic
      workload the threshold holds at, which is never written into the budgets file).
      `evidence` (string, where the number came from: a spike report's id and figures, or
      the measurement it rests on). `command` (string, the command that analyses the
      telemetry the gate's tests record and reports through the onebudgetspec SDK, as it
      will be registered; it runs no scenario of its own only to measure, save under the
      standalone-measurement exception, which is `direct`). The same list is the task's
      `orchestrator.budgets` metadata. Newly authored records also have `schema_version`
      (integer literal 3; `2` stays readable), `source` (string, `direct` or `telemetry`)
      and `check_runtime_seconds` (finite number >= 0, excluding booleans). Direct executes
      the work/check it measures, including commands recording their result; telemetry
      reads existing timing/history records without executing measured work.
      `check_runtime_seconds` is the seconds checking this budget adds to the repository's
      checks at its workload: the telemetry collection it adds to tests the work needs
      anyway plus the budget command's own run, or, where a test exists only to feed this
      budget, that whole test's runtime plus the command. It never counts tests that would
      exist without the budget, and it is distinct from target, unit and basis. Evidence
      states the estimate's source. Never infer either field from basis or command. A
      version-3 record whose `file_change` is `change` also has `previous` (object), the
      budget as it stood before this task, with exactly the keys `name`, `measure`,
      `inner_measure_reason`, `unit`, `direction`, `threshold`, `workload`, `source`,
      `command` and `check_runtime_seconds`, each typed and constrained as the record's own
      key of that name, its `check_runtime_seconds` what checking the entry cost before the
      change; one whose `file_change` is `add` or `none` has no `previous`. Version-2
      records and exact legacy keys remain readable, with no `previous`.
    type: list
    items: object
    default: []
    schema:
      type: array
      items:
        type: object
        additionalProperties: false
        required: [id, name, basis, repository, file, file_change, measure, inner_measure_reason, unit, direction, threshold, workload, evidence, command]
        dependentRequired:
          schema_version: [source, check_runtime_seconds]
        # A version-3 change carries `previous`; nothing else may.
        if: {required: [schema_version], properties: {schema_version: {const: 3}}}
        then:
          if: {properties: {file_change: {const: change}}}
          then: {required: [previous]}
          else: {properties: {previous: false}}
        else: {properties: {previous: false}}
        properties:
          schema_version: {enum: [2, 3]}
          id: {type: string, pattern: "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"}
          name: &name {type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 60, pattern: "^[^\\n]*$"}
          basis: {enum: [measured, arithmetic, design, published docs, estimate]}
          repository: {type: string, minLength: 1}
          file: {type: string, pattern: "(^|/)budgets\\.yaml$"}
          file_change: {enum: [add, change, none]}
          measure: &measure {type: string, minLength: 1}
          inner_measure_reason: &inner_measure_reason {type: string}
          unit: &unit {type: string, minLength: 1}
          direction: &direction {enum: [max, min]}
          threshold: &threshold {type: number}
          workload: &workload {type: string, minLength: 1}
          evidence: {type: string, minLength: 1}
          command: &command {type: string, minLength: 1}
          source: &source {enum: [direct, telemetry]}
          check_runtime_seconds: &check_runtime_seconds {type: number, minimum: 0}
          previous:
            type: object
            additionalProperties: false
            required: [name, measure, inner_measure_reason, unit, direction, threshold, workload, source, command, check_runtime_seconds]
            properties:
              name: *name
              measure: *measure
              inner_measure_reason: *inner_measure_reason
              unit: *unit
              direction: *direction
              threshold: *threshold
              workload: *workload
              source: *source
              command: *command
              check_runtime_seconds: *check_runtime_seconds
  # llmlint: ignore-end[contracts_have_one_source_or_a_drift_gate]
---
{#-
  THE READERS. The worker this task dispatches, its judge, and a person following a design
  document's link to this section. The heading is exactly `## Budgets`, so the section's
  anchor is `budgets`. A versioned (schema 2 or 3) budget's own heading is `Budget <id>`,
  plain Markdown and no raw HTML, which a public copy of the task may carry: its slug is the
  anchor GitHub's heading slug of `Budget <id>`, because this template's schema holds the id
  to onebudgetspec's id pattern. A legacy budget's heading is its name. A version-3 changed
  budget shows each `previous` value beside the new one, which is where a design document's
  changed-budget line sends its reader for the full before and after.
-#}
{% macro target(one) %}{% if one.direction == "max" %}at most{% elif one.direction == "min" %}at least{% else %}{{ one.direction }}{% endif %} {{ one.threshold }} {{ one.unit }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro command(text) %}{% if "`" in text %}{{ text }}{% else %}`{{ text }}`{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro before(value) %}{{ "\n" }}  - **Before this task:** {{ value }}{% endmacro %}
{% if budgets %}
## Budgets

{% for budget in budgets %}
{% set version = budget.schema_version | default(0) %}
{% set was = budget.previous if (version == 3 and budget.previous is defined) else none %}
{% if version in [2, 3] %}
### Budget {{ budget.id }}

- **Name:** {{ budget.name }}{% if was %}{{ before(was.name) }}{% endif %}

{% else %}
### {{ budget.name }}

{% endif %}
- **Id:** `{{ budget.id }}`
- **Measure:** {{ budget.measure }}{% if was %}{{ before(was.measure) }}{% endif %}

{% if budget.inner_measure_reason or (was and was.inner_measure_reason) %}
- **Inner measure, because:** {{ budget.inner_measure_reason or "none" }}{% if was %}{{ before(was.inner_measure_reason or "none") }}{% endif %}

{% endif %}
- **Target:** {{ target(budget) }}{% if was %}{{ before(target(was)) }}{% endif %}

- **Basis:** {{ budget.basis }}
{% if version in [2, 3] %}
- **Measurement source:** {{ budget.source }}{% if was %}{{ before(was.source) }}{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% if version == 3 %}
- **Check runtime added:** approximately {{ budget.check_runtime_seconds }} seconds{% if was %}{{ before("approximately " ~ was.check_runtime_seconds ~ " seconds") }}{% endif %}

{% elif version == 2 %}
- **Check runtime:** approximately {{ budget.check_runtime_seconds }} seconds
{% endif %}
- **Workload:** {{ budget.workload }}{% if was %}{{ before(was.workload) }}{% endif %}

- **Evidence:** {{ budget.evidence }}
- **Command:** {{ command(budget.command) }}{% if was %}{{ before(command(was.command)) }}{% endif %}

- **Registered in:** `{{ budget.file }}` of `{{ budget.repository }}`, {% if budget.file_change == "add" %}an entry this task adds{% elif budget.file_change == "change" %}an entry this task changes{% elif budget.file_change == "none" %}an entry this task leaves as it is{% else %}{{ budget.file_change }}{% endif %}


{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
